terminant of a 2x2 Matrix With Integer Entries","answers":[{"id":62404196,"created":"2026-10-16T20:10:41.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13265,"number":1,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 8:10 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:13","question":{"id":1071,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":4434,"text":"<p>$\n \\left|\n\\begin{array}{cc} \n\t6 & 3 \\\\\n\t2 & 1\n\\end{array}\n\\right|\n=\n$</p>\n","choice1":"$0$","choice2":"$16$","choice3":"$9$","choice4":"$3$","choice5":"$2$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>For a $2 \\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula</p>\n<p>\\[\n\\begin{vmatrix} a & b \\\\ c & d \\end{vmatrix} = ad - bc.\n\\]</p>\n<p>Using the formula, we have:</p>\n<p>\\begin{align}\n\t\\left|\n\t\\begin{array}{cc} \n\t\t6 & 3 \\\\\n\t\t2 & 1\n\t\\end{array}\n\t\\right|\n\n\t& =\n\n\t6 \\cdot 1 - 3 \\cdot 2\\\\[5pt]\n       &  = 6 - 6 \\\\[5pt]\n       & = 0\n\\end{align}</p>\n","topic":{"id":152,"name":"The Determinant of a 2x2 Matrix"},"example":{"id":4434,"title":"Calculating the Determinant of a 2x2 Matrix With Integer Entries"},"group":{"id":92272,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[{"id":null,"number":null,"answers":[]}],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14272902,"answer":{"id":62404196,"cread":"2026-10-16T20:10:41.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13265},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62404202,"created":"2026-10-16T20:10:56.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":null,"freeResponse":"[\"18\"]","timeElapsed":11215,"number":2,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 8:10 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:11","question":{"id":317341,"format":"FR","difficulty":1,"exampleId":4434,"text":"Evaluate the determinant:","choice1":null,"choice2":null,"choice3":null,"choice4":null,"choice5":null,"freeAnswerChoice":"\\newline\n$\n\\begin{vmatrix}\n7 & 2 \\\\\n5 & 4\n\\end{vmatrix} =\n$\n[\n    answer: 18;\n    type: number;\n    width: 35;\n    margin-left: 2;\n    margin-right: 1;\n    buttons: frac;\n]","explanation":"<p>For a $2 \\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula</p>\n<p>\\[\n\\begin{vmatrix} a & b \\\\ c & d \\end{vmatrix} = ad - bc.\n\\]</p>\n<p>Using the formula, we have\n\\begin{align*}\n\\left|\n\\begin{array}{cc} \n7 & 2 \\\\\n5 & 4\n\\end{array}\n\\right|\n& = 7 \\cdot 4 - 2 \\cdot 5 \\\\[5pt]\n& = 28 - 10 \\\\[5pt]\n& = \\bbox[4pt,border: 1px solid lightgray]{18}.\n\\end{align*}</p>\n","topic":{"id":152,"name":"The Determinant of a 2x2 Matrix"},"example":{"id":4434,"title":"Calculating the Determinant of a 2x2 Matrix With Integer Entries"},"group":{"id":92271,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14272902,"answer":{"id":62404202,"cread":"2026-10-16T20:10:56.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":null,"freeResponse":["18"],"timeElapsed":11215},"graphic":false,"freeResponse":{"segments":[{"newline":true},{"text":"$\n\\begin{vmatrix}\n7 & 2 \\\\\n5 & 4\n\\end{vmatrix} =\n$\n"},{"textbox":{"answer":"18","type":"number","width":35,"margin":{"left":2,"right":1},"buttons":["frac"]}}]},"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}}]},{"id":4435,"number":2,"title":"Calculating the Determinant of a 2x2 Matrix With Non-Integer Entries","answers":[{"id":62404215,"created":"2026-10-16T20:11:20.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":null,"freeResponse":"[\"3x^2+10y\"]","timeElapsed":15323,"number":3,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 8:11 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:15","question":{"id":317372,"format":"FR","difficulty":2,"exampleId":4435,"text":"Calculate $\\det(D)$ given that\n$ D  = \n\\begin{bmatrix}\n3x & 2y \\\\\n-5 & x\n\\end{bmatrix}.\n$","choice1":null,"choice2":null,"choice3":null,"choice4":null,"choice5":null,"freeAnswerChoice":"\\newline\n$\\det(D) =$\n[\n    answer: 3x^2+10y;\n    type: expression;\n    width: 80;\n    margin-left: 2;\n    margin-right: 1;\n    buttons: frac, exp;\n]","explanation":"<p>For a $2 \\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula</p>\n<p>\\[\n\\begin{vmatrix} a & b \\\\ c & d \\end{vmatrix} = ad - bc.\n\\]</p>\n<p>Using the formula, we have\n\\begin{align*}\n\\text{det}(D) & =\n\\begin{vmatrix}\n3x & 2y \\\\\n-5 & x\n\\end{vmatrix} \\\\[5pt]\n\n&= 3x \\cdot x - 2y \\cdot (-5) \\\\[5pt]\n\n&= \\bbox[4pt,border: 1px solid lightgray]{3x^2 + 10y}.\n\\end{align*}</p>\n","topic":{"id":152,"name":"The Determinant of a 2x2 Matrix"},"example":{"id":4435,"title":"Calculating the Determinant of a 2x2 Matrix With Non-Integer Entries"},"group":{"id":92287,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14272902,"answer":{"id":62404215,"cread":"2026-10-16T20:11:20.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":null,"freeResponse":["3x^2+10y"],"timeElapsed":15323},"graphic":false,"freeResponse":{"segments":[{"newline":true},{"text":"$\\det(D) =$\n"},{"textbox":{"answer":"3x^2+10y","type":"expression","width":80,"margin":{"left":2,"right":1},"buttons":["frac","exp"]}}]},"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62404225,"created":"2026-10-16T20:11:37.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":null,"freeResponse":"[\"-5\\\\sqrt{3}\"]","timeElapsed":12074,"number":4,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 8:11 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:12","question":{"id":317369,"format":"FR","difficulty":1,"exampleId":4435,"text":"Evaluate the determinant:","choice1":null,"choice2":null,"choice3":null,"choice4":null,"choice5":null,"freeAnswerChoice":"\\newline\n$\n\\begin{vmatrix}\n    -\\sqrt{3} & 4 \\\\\n    \\sqrt{3} & 1\n\\end{vmatrix}\n= $\n[\n    answer: -5\\sqrt{3};\n    type: expression;\n    width: 60;\n    margin-left: 2;\n    margin-right: 1;\n    buttons: sqrt, frac;\n]","explanation":"<p>For a $2 \\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula</p>\n<p>\\[\n\\begin{vmatrix} a & b \\\\ c & d \\end{vmatrix} = ad - bc.\n\\]</p>\n<p>Using the formula, we have\n\\begin{align*}\n\\begin{vmatrix}\n    -\\sqrt{3} & 4 \\\\\n    \\sqrt{3} & 1\n\\end{vmatrix}\n& = -\\sqrt{3} \\cdot 1 - 4 \\cdot \\sqrt{3} \\\\[5pt]\n& = -\\sqrt{3} - 4\\sqrt{3} \\\\[5pt]\n& = \\bbox[4pt,border: 1px solid lightgray]{-5\\sqrt{3}}.\n\\end{align*}</p>\n","topic":{"id":152,"name":"The Determinant of a 2x2 Matrix"},"example":{"id":4435,"title":"Calculating the Determinant of a 2x2 Matrix With Non-Integer Entries"},"group":{"id":92285,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14272902,"answer":{"id":62404225,"cread":"2026-10-16T20:11:37.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":null,"freeResponse":["-5\\sqrt{3}"],"timeElapsed":12074},"graphic":false,"freeResponse":{"segments":[{"newline":true},{"text":"$\n\\begin{vmatrix}\n    -\\sqrt{3} & 4 \\\\\n    \\sqrt{3} & 1\n\\end{vmatrix}\n= $\n"},{"textbox":{"answer":"-5\\sqrt{3}","type":"expression","width":60,"margin":{"left":2,"right":1},"buttons":["frac","sqrt"]}}]},"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}}]},{"id":4436,"number":3,"title":"Solving for an Unknown in an Expression Involving the Determinant of a 2x2 Matrix","answers":[{"id":62404237,"created":"2026-10-16T20:11:57.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":11500,"number":5,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 8:11 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:12","question":{"id":127606,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":4436,"text":"<p>If\n$\n    T =\n    \\begin{bmatrix}\n       v& 2v \\\\\n        2 & v+8\n    \\end{bmatrix}\n$\nand $\\det(T) = -4$, what is the value of $v?$</p>\n","choice1":"$v=-2$","choice2":"$v=\\dfrac{7}{3}$","choice3":"$v=4$","choice4":"$v=\\dfrac{3}{4}$","choice5":"$v=-3$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>For a $2 \\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula</p>\n<p>\\[\n\\begin{vmatrix} a & b \\\\ c & d \\end{vmatrix} = ad - bc.\n\\]</p>\n<p>Using the formula, we have:</p>\n<p>\\begin{align}\n\t\t\\det(T) &= \n\t\t\\begin{vmatrix}\n       v& 2v \\\\\n        2 & v+8\n    \t\t\\end{vmatrix} \\\\[5pt]\n\t\t&= v\\cdot (v+8)-2v\\cdot 2 \\\\[5pt]\n\t\t&= v^2+4v \n\\end{align}</p>\n<p>Since $\\det(T)=-4$, we obtain:</p>\n<p>\\begin{align}\n\\det(T) &= -4 \\\\[3pt]\nv^2+4v & = -4 \\\\[3pt]\nv^2+4v+4 & = 0 \\\\[3pt]\n%t^2 - 6t + 9 & = 0 \\\\[3pt]\n(v+2)^2 &= 0 \\\\[3pt]\nv & = -2\n\\end{align}</p>\n","topic":{"id":152,"name":"The Determinant of a 2x2 Matrix"},"example":{"id":4436,"title":"Solving for an Unknown in an Expression Involving the Determinant of a 2x2 Matrix"},"group":{"id":92297,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14272902,"answer":{"id":62404237,"cread":"2026-10-16T20:11:57.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":11500},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62404248,"created":"2026-10-16T20:12:14.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":11374,"number":6,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 8:12 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:11","question":{"id":69658,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":4436,"text":"<p>If\n    $\n    U = \n    \\left\\lbrack\n    \\matrix {\n       - v & 5 \\\\\n        4 & 3\n    }\n    \\right\\rbrack\n    $\nand\n$\\text{det}({U}) = 4$, what is the value of $v?$</p>\n","choice1":"$-8$","choice2":"$4$","choice3":"$8$","choice4":"$6$","choice5":"$-9$","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>For a $2 \\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula</p>\n<p>\\[\n\\begin{vmatrix} a & b \\\\ c & d \\end{vmatrix} = ad - bc.\n\\]</p>\n<p>Using the formula, we have:</p>\n<p>\\begin{align}\n\\text{det}({U}) \n\n& =\n\\left|\n    \\matrix {\n          -v & 5 \\\\\n          4 & 3\n\t  }\n\\right| \\\\[5pt]\n\n& =-v \\cdot 3 - 5 \\cdot 4 \\\\[5pt]\n\n&  = -3v - 20\n\\end{align}</p>\n<p>Since $\\det(U) = 4$, we get:</p>\n<p>\\begin{align}\n\\det(U) &= 4 \\\\[3pt]\n-3v - 20 & = 4 \\\\[3pt]\n-3v         & = 4 + 20 \\\\[3pt]\n-3v         & = 24 \\\\[3pt]\nv           & = -8\n\\end{align}     </p>\n","topic":{"id":152,"name":"The Determinant of a 2x2 Matrix"},"example":{"id":4436,"title":"Solving for an Unknown in an Expression Involving the Determinant of a 2x2 Matrix"},"group":{"id":92293,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14272902,"answer":{"id":62404248,"cread":"2026-10-16T20:12:14.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":11374},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}}]}],"localGraph":{"topicId":152,"topics":[{"id":66,"name":"Solving Two-Step Equations","prerequisites":[],"frontier":0,"halfLife":999999999.0000005,"repetition":29,"stability":1},{"id":152,"name":"The Determinant of a 2x2 Matrix","prerequisites":[66,352,353,362,861],"frontier":0,"halfLife":61.20245723153326,"repetition":5,"stability":0.7406107626222461},{"id":233,"name":"The Minors of a 3x3 Matrix","prerequisites":[152],"frontier":1,"halfLife":0.1,"repetition":0,"stability":0},{"id":352,"name":"Factoring Perfect Square Trinomials","prerequisites":[],"frontier":0,"halfLife":999999999.0000005,"repetition":29,"stability":1},{"id":353,"name":"Factoring Polynomials Using GCFs","prerequisites":[],"frontier":0,"halfLife":999999999.0000005,"repetition":29,"stability":1},{"id":362,"name":"The Power Rule for Exponents With Algebraic Expressions","prerequisites":[],"frontier":0,"halfLife":999999999.0000005,"repetition":29,"stability":1},{"id":861,"name":"Introduction to Matrices","prerequisites":[],"frontier":0,"halfLife":146.97393579562095,"repetition":6,"stability":0.95126